# Force LF everywhere, regardless of a contributor's local core.autocrlf
# setting. Without this, a Windows checkout can materialize every text
# file with CRLF line endings, which Prettier (and CI, which always runs
# on Linux) then flags as a formatting violation on an otherwise-untouched
# file — exactly the class of "works on my machine" bug this file exists
# to rule out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish or generated files: never touch their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
